// A token that has to be there, consumed. A declaration must initialise
// (`int x = 1`, never `int x`) and a case's tuple must close: the token is the
// caller's, not a function per token.
eat_text(int[] pos, string want) {
  expect_text(pos, want);
  advance(pos);
} return void;
